//! task: write
//! ask: Write a function that writes a textus to a Scriptor, requiring exactly whatever authority the writer carries.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §4.2, examples/imprime.exsc
//! explain: The row is deliberately not `poscit archivum`. The authority comes from the writer that was handed in, so the function requires exactly what its `Scriptor` requires and nothing more. Point it at a writer holding `ambitus` and it requires `ambitus`; point it at one holding nothing and it requires nothing. The function does not decide and does not have to guess.

publica functio imprime_gutenbergio(s: Scriptor, t: textus) -> mensura poscit sicut s {
    redde s.scribe(t);
}
